      \HLAFrontPageThreeLine{\hspace*{-1.50pt}\textbf{Abstract:} The High Level Architecture (HLA) has been developed to provide a common}
      \HLAFrontPageThreeLine{architecture for distributed modeling and simulation. The HLA defines an integrated approach that}
      \HLAFrontPageThreeLine{provides a common framework for the interconnection of interacting simulations. This standard,}
      \HLAFrontPageThreeLine{describing the framework and rules of the High Level Architecture (HLA), is the capstone}
      \HLAFrontPageThreeLine{document for a family of related HLA standards. It defines the HLA, its components, and the rules}
      \HLAFrontPageThreeLine{that outline the responsibilities of HLA federates and federations to ensure a consistent}
      \HLAFrontPageThreeLine{implementation. Simulations are abstractions of the real world, and no one simulation can solve}
      \HLAFrontPageThreeLine{all of the functional needs for the modeling and simulation community. It is anticipated that}
      \HLAFrontPageThreeLine{technology advances will allow for new and different modeling and simulation (M\&S)}
      \HLAFrontPageThreeLine{implementations within the framework of the HLA. The standards contained in this architecture}
      \HLAFrontPageThreeLine{are interrelated and need to be considered as a product set when changes are made. They each}
      have value independently.\par\vspace{11.4pt}
      \HLAFrontPageThreeLine{\textbf{Keywords:} architecture, class attribute, federate, federation, federation execution, federation}
